26	 * Kept separate from the owner controller and the {@code Owner} model so the rule for deciding when
27	 * two owners belong to the same household lives in one place, as pure functions with no web or
28	 * persistence dependencies. Mirrors {@link TelephoneNormalizer}, which does the same for telephones.
29	 *
30	 * <p>Two owners share a household when their {@linkplain #toComparisonKey(String, String) comparison
31	 * keys} are equal. The last name is reduced for comparison by trimming, collapsing every run of
32	 * whitespace to a single space and lower-casing, so households recorded in different letter cases or
33	 * with incidental spacing still compare equal (e.g. {@code "  Franklin "} / {@code "2000"} matches
34	 * {@code "franklin"} / {@code "2000"}); the postcode is a fixed 4-digit code and is compared as
35	 * given.
36	 */
